WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.258
FastAPI applications usually run as ASGI
applications,

2
00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:11.583
which means the application may sit behind
an ASGI server, a reverse proxy,

3
00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:14.339
a load balancer, an API gateway,

4
00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:19.672
or other infrastructure before a request
reaches Python code.

5
00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:24.807
Routers help organize path operations by
feature or domain,

6
00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:28.654
but architecture is more than folder
layout.

7
00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:35.573
A secure structure makes authentication,
authorization, validation, logging,

8
00:00:35.653 --> 00:00:41.006
and error handling consistent across the
routes that need them.

9
00:00:41.086 --> 00:00:44.952
Configuration should be environment-aware.

10
00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:52.169
Development settings often favor
convenience, local credentials, verbose errors,

11
00:00:52.249 --> 00:00:54.627
and visible documentation.

12
00:00:54.707 --> 00:00:58.276
Production settings need safer defaults,

13
00:00:58.356 --> 00:01:05.096
controlled host and proxy assumptions,
private secrets, predictable logging,

14
00:01:05.176 --> 00:01:08.844
and deliberate exposure of documentation.

15
00:01:08.924 --> 00:01:15.961
Debug behavior and interactive API
documentation can be useful for development and

16
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:22.881
internal environments, but teams should
decide intentionally what is exposed in

17
00:01:22.961 --> 00:01:25.637
production and who can reach it.

18
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:29.186
Secrets should live outside source code.

19
00:01:29.266 --> 00:01:35.610
API keys, token signing material, database
credentials, webhook secrets,

20
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:41.241
and service credentials should not be
committed to repositories,

21
00:01:41.321 --> 00:01:44.592
copied into images, or printed in logs.

22
00:01:44.672 --> 00:01:48.538
Configuration validation is also
important.

23
00:01:48.618 --> 00:01:55.457
The application should fail clearly at
startup if required security settings are

24
00:01:55.537 --> 00:02:02.079
missing or unsafe, rather than running
with defaults that were never meant for

25
00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:03.249
production.

26
00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:07.889
Deployment boundaries affect security
assumptions.

27
00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:14.015
A proxy may terminate TLS, set forwarding
headers, enforce body limits,

28
00:02:14.095 --> 00:02:16.871
or identify the original client.

29
00:02:16.951 --> 00:02:23.592
The FastAPI application still needs to
know which headers are trusted and which

30
00:02:23.672 --> 00:02:26.249
hosts or origins are expected.

31
00:02:26.329 --> 00:02:33.664
Configuration should document those
assumptions so the service behaves consistently

32
00:02:33.744 --> 00:02:40.980
across local development, staging,
production, and cloud or container deployments.
